//? Title: Convolution as Patch Extraction and GEMM
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Applying one filter to every image location repeats the same local dot product. We expose
those patches as a tensor matrix, multiply by a reshaped filter and compare forward and
backward results with convolution. An overlap map explains why patch extraction's adjoint
adds contributions rather than simply reshaping them.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.1_fundamentals/convolution_im2col.cpp`.

> The method

For NHWC input X, im2col makes one row per batch/output location and one column per
kernel-row/kernel-column/input-channel coordinate. A HWIO filter becomes W with shape
[kh kw Cin,Cout]. Cross-correlation is Y=PW; the spatial filter is not reversed.

$$
\frac{\partial L}{\partial W}=P^TG,\qquad
\frac{\partial L}{\partial P}=GW^T,\qquad
\frac{\partial L}{\partial X}=E^T\operatorname{vec}(GW^T).
$$
\alttext(Filter gradients multiply patches transposed by upstream gradients; input gradients apply the patch-extraction adjoint.)

E is the sparse patch-selection matrix. The adjoint Eᵀ scatter-adds each patch coordinate
back to its source pixel. Thus EᵀE is diagonal with coverage counts, not generally identity.
The implementation uses differentiable sliding-window views, followed by a materialised
matrix reshape. Padding, stride and dilation use convolution's geometry; SAME puts any odd
extra zero after the image. Patch storage is O(N Ho Wo kh kw Cin); the matrix product takes
O(N Ho Wo kh kw Cin Cout). The reference path targets clarity, not a memory-saving kernel.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/convolution_im2col_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/convolution_im2col_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/convolution_im2col_concept.tikz > build/convolution_im2col_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/convolution_im2col_concept.svg build/convolution_im2col_concept.dvi > build/convolution_im2col_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
